ID: vr-28
Title: Optional monochrome Claire and matching-format hair in every view
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/27

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Preserve Claire while offering color-free rendering and opt-in hair across presentations.
Dependencies: vr-20, vr-21, vr-22, vr-23, vr-24, vr-25

Purpose:
Let the owner disable Claire's added colors and use any existing hairstyle
with FaceMesh, FaceDot and UniformPolygons, rendered like the selected head.

Tasks:
[x] Add a reversible Claire Colors option covering skin, cosmetics, eyes and hair.
[x] Expose shared hairstyle selection and remember hair visibility per view.
[x] Default other views to hair off; match wire/dot/grid geometry and occlusion.
[x] Fit optional hair, preserve curved crop and support the native floating tab.
[x] Verify real pixels, restoration, audio ownership, bounded work and defaults.
[ ] Update book/guide/README/tracking and publish verified source as Zanark.

Acceptance criteria:
Claire's existing appearance/hair defaults stay unchanged. Colors off produces
neutral grayscale head/eyes/hair in either Claire material without replacing
motion, regenerating or seeking speech. Re-enabling restores original pixels.
All eleven hairstyle options work in every implemented view; one shared style,
independent per-view Hair choices, default off for the three additional views.
FaceMesh hair uses triangle edges, FaceDot only surface dots, UniformPolygons
only rectangular grid outlines. Invisible depth surfaces occlude rear marks.
Hair/face rotate together and share dot/grid density/gap and applicable crop.
Hair-enabled fitting includes its actual extent without per-frame scans or
unbounded geometry/style caches. Returning to hair-off restores original fit.
Reload resets unsaved settings. Preserve native sandbox/capability boundaries,
one audio/renderer owner and no device/profile/sibling-app access.

